Keep the fast WebGPU paths that were measured on NVIDIA off the other vendors.

The 0009 guard turns vec flash-attn off through the probed subgroup width
only. A Dawn D3D12 path can probe 32 while the hardware still runs wave64,
so the guard can pass on a GCN device and leave decode on the vec kernel,
whose variable-delta subgroupShuffleDown is the pattern wave64 has
miscompiled. The correctness probe now also reads the adapter vendor, the
same string 0010 gates the mat-vec workgroup on. A vendor other than nvidia
gets the tile shader for decode. NVIDIA keeps the measured RTX 4090 paths
and pays one string compare; no probe or kernel is added for it.

The 0012 argmax node also runs on every vendor although it was measured on
NVIDIA only, and a wrong index is a wrong token. The graph gets that node
only when the output device is this backend with an nvidia adapter, which
the new ggml_backend_webgpu_dev_is_nvidia() reports. Other vendors read the
logits back and scan them on the CPU, the sampling of v1.3.0.

The probe log carries the vendor next to the vec=on/off it already printed.
The degenerate-output detector and the per-piece CPU retry of #63 stay
unchanged, so a broken decode still falls back instead of showing garbage.

